# Components

A file contains one React component. Export it as a named function. That name is what React shows in DevTools.

A control that is only a button ends with `Button`, such as `FetchStreamsButton`. Two handlers that only set a boolean on and off are one toggle: `setOpen((open) => !open)`.

Render a memo child directly. Do not assign `<FetchStreamsButton />` to `useMemo`. Wrap the component in `memo` only when the memoization rule says the skip pays off.

```tsx
/** Centered column for one page. */
export function Page({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  return <section>{children}</section>;
}
```
